  "result": "Perfect! All 214 tests pass. The credit note functionality is now fully implemented with 17 comprehensive tests:\n\n**Created `src/credits.js`:**\n- **`createCreditNote(invoice, { amount, reason, date }, existingNumbers)`** creates credit notes for refunds\n  - Validates invoice status is 'issued', 'partially_paid', or 'paid' (returns NOT_ISSUED for draft)\n  - Validates date is valid (returns DATE_INVALID if not)\n  - Validates amount is positive integer (returns AMOUNT_INVALID otherwise)\n  - Validates amount does not exceed invoice total (returns CREDIT_TOO_HIGH if exceeded)\n  - Returns `ok({ number, invoiceNumber, customerId, amount, reason, date })`\n  - Credit note numbers use CN-YYYY-NNNN format with separate counter from invoices\n\n**Updated `src/numbering.js`:**\n- Added `nextCreditNoteNumber(existingNumbers, date)` - generates CN numbers with year-based counter reset\n\n**Updated `src/errors.js`:**\n- Added CREDIT_TOO_HIGH error code\n\n**Test coverage (17 new tests):**\n- Creates credit note for issued invoice\n- Generates CN number with CN prefix\n- Separate counter for credit notes vs invoices\n- Rejects draft invoices (NOT_ISSUED)\n- Accepts issued, partially_paid, and paid invoices\n- Rejects invalid dates\n- Rejects non-integer, zero, and negative amounts\n- Rejects amounts exceeding invoice total\n- Allows amounts equal to invoice total\n- Counter resets by year\n- Works with invoices having line discounts\n- Works with invoices having vouchers\n- Includes existing invoice numbers in numbering\n\nAll 214 tests pass (197 existing + 17 new).",
